Package: ashgswuw
Title: Weighted Usable Width from Reach-Average Channel Geometry (ASHGS Direct-Geometry Pathway)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("M. J.", "Bayly", email = "mjbayly@mjbayly.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An independent R adaptation of selected functions from the
    At-a-Station Hydraulic Geometry Simulator (ASHGS). The original ASHGS was
    written in MATLAB by Dr. Brett Eaton (University of British Columbia) and
    is distributed under GPL-3 at <https://blogs.ubc.ca/beaton/working-code/>;
    the method was developed and published by Daniel McParland, Brett Eaton
    and Jordan Rosenfeld (2016) <doi:10.1002/rra.2851>. Credit for the
    method and the original code belongs to them. They have not reviewed or
    endorsed this package, and any errors in the adaptation are the package
    author's alone. Estimates weighted usable width (WUW, m) and, optionally,
    weighted usable area (WUA, m2) of fish habitat at a given discharge from
    reach-average bankfull width, mean bankfull depth, reach gradient, D84 and
    user-supplied depth and velocity habitat suitability curves. Only the
    hydraulic-geometry and habitat components were adapted, with the
    corrections documented in the package README; sediment transport, the UBC
    Regime Model and all plotting from the original tools are omitted. Channel
    geometry is assumed fixed.
